.TH TETRISPLUS 6 "2026" "tetrisplus" "Games"
.SH NAME
tetrisplus \- a Tetris game for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tetrisplus
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tetrisplus
is a complete Tetris game that runs in a terminal, written in C against
ncurses.
.PP
It opens on a menu where you pick a game mode and an action, then plays in a
full\(hyscreen view showing the falling piece, a ghost marking where a hard
drop would land, a next\(hypiece preview, and the live score, level and line
counters.
.PP
Your terminal must be at least 50 columns by 22 rows. Smaller terminals show a
notice instead of a broken screen, and the layout recentres itself whenever you
resize.
.SH CONTROLS
.SS In the menu
.TP
.B Up / Down
Move between actions.
.TP
.B Left / Right
Switch game mode.
.TP
.B Enter
Confirm the highlighted action.
.TP
.B Q
Quit.
.SS In a game
.TP
.B Left / Right
Move the piece sideways.
.TP
.B Up
Rotate clockwise.
.TP
.B Down
Soft drop, worth one point per cell.
.TP
.B Space
Hard drop, worth two points per cell.
.TP
.B P
Pause or resume.
.TP
.B M
Return to the main menu, abandoning the current run.
.TP
.B Q
Quit to the shell.
.SS When a run ends
.TP
.B R
Play again in the same mode.
.TP
.B M
Back to the main menu.
.TP
.B Q
Quit.
.SS Entering your initials
If a score reaches the top ten you are prompted for three initials.
Letters and digits are accepted; Backspace deletes; Enter saves; Esc skips the
prompt without saving.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B Marathon
Endless. Survive and score. Ranked by score.
.TP
.B Sprint
Clear 40 lines as fast as you can. Ranked by time, fastest first. A time is
recorded only if all 40 lines are actually cleared.
.TP
.B Ultra
Two minutes on the clock. Score as much as you can. Ranked by score.
.TP
.B Expert
Endless, but starting at level 10, so gravity opens at 170 ms per step rather
than 800 ms. Ranked by score.
.PP
Gravity ramps from 800 ms per step down to a floor of 80 ms, and the level
rises every 10 lines. Any mode with an objective swaps the level readout for a
clock: counting up in Sprint, down in Ultra.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/tetrisplus/scores
Persistent high scores, one entry per line, kept per mode. Falls back to
.IR ~/.local/share/tetrisplus/scores
when
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
is unset. The directory is created on demand; if it cannot be written the game
still plays, it just does not remember scores.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Nothing is printed to the terminal outside the curses screen, so
.B tetrisplus
is safe to launch with its output redirected. Errors writing the score file are
deliberately swallowed so a bad score table can never stop the game from being
playable.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation in
.IR /usr/share/doc/tetrisplus/README.md .
